@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Security & Privacy";
}

<div class="container py-4">

    @* Заглавие и предназначение на страницата *@
    <div class="bg-light rounded-4 p-4 p-md-5 mb-4">
        <h1 class="fw-bold">Security & Privacy</h1>

        <p class="lead mb-2">
            Secure sharing and management of public
            SSL/TLS certificates.
        </p>

        <p class="text-muted mb-0">
            Learn how SecureCert Portal processes certificate
            submissions, protects access and handles user data.
        </p>
    </div>

    @* 1. Предназначение на платформата *@
    <section class="mb-4">
        <h3>1. About SecureCert Portal</h3>

        <p>
            SecureCert Portal is a web application for
            submitting, validating and reviewing public
            SSL/TLS certificates between organizations.
        </p>

        <p>
            Client organizations can submit certificates
            and track their review status.
            Authorized administrators manage organizations,
            client accounts and certificate reviews.
        </p>
    </section>

    <hr />

    @* 2. Разрешени файлови формати *@
    <section class="mb-4">
        <h3>2. Accepted Certificate Files</h3>

        <p>
            The portal accepts public X.509 certificates
            in the following formats:
        </p>

        <div class="row g-3 mb-3">

            <div class="col-md-4">
                <div class="card h-100">
                    <div class="card-body">
                        <h5>.cer</h5>
                        <p class="text-muted mb-0">
                            Public certificate file.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="col-md-4">
                <div class="card h-100">
                    <div class="card-body">
                        <h5>.crt</h5>
                        <p class="text-muted mb-0">
                            Public certificate file.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="col-md-4">
                <div class="card h-100">
                    <div class="card-body">
                        <h5>.pem</h5>
                        <p class="text-muted mb-0">
                            PEM-encoded public certificate.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

        </div>

        <p>
            <strong>Maximum file size:</strong> 256 KB.
        </p>

        <div class="alert alert-info">
            A certificate must be submitted for the hostname
            entered in the upload form.
        </div>
    </section>

    <hr />

    @* 3. Техническа проверка на сертификатите *@
    <section class="mb-4">
        <h3>3. Certificate Validation</h3>

        <p>
            Before a certificate is accepted, SecureCert
            Portal performs technical validation.
        </p>

        <ul>
            <li>
                Checks the supported file format and file size.
            </li>
            <li>
                Parses the public X.509 certificate.
            </li>
            <li>
                Checks the certificate validity period.
            </li>
            <li>
                Checks whether the certificate matches
                the submitted hostname.
            </li>
            <li>
                Checks server authentication usage
                when the relevant extension is present.
            </li>
            <li>
                Extracts certificate metadata, including
                subject, issuer, thumbprint and validity dates.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <div class="alert alert-warning">
            <strong>Important:</strong>
            Technical validation does not establish that the
            issuing Certificate Authority is trusted.
            The current version does not perform complete
            certificate chain or revocation validation.
        </div>
    </section>

    <hr />

    @* 4. Защита на частните ключове *@
    <section class="mb-4">
        <h3>4. Private Key Protection</h3>

        <div class="alert alert-danger">
            <strong>Never upload a private key.</strong>

            Do not submit private key files, passwords,
            credentials or certificate packages containing
            private key material.
        </div>

        <p>
            The portal is intended for public certificates
            only. Private keys must remain under the control
            of their legitimate owner.
        </p>

        <p>
            Files such as .key, .pfx and .p12 are not
            supported certificate submission formats.
        </p>
    </section>

    <hr />

    @* 5. Роли и достъп *@
    <section class="mb-4">
        <h3>5. User Access & Authorization</h3>

        <div class="table-responsive">
            <table class="table table-bordered">

                <thead class="table-light">
                    <tr>
                        <th>Role</th>
                        <th>Access</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>

                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>Administrator</strong></td>
                        <td>
                            Manages organizations, client
                            users and certificate reviews.
                        </td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>Client</strong></td>
                        <td>
                            Uploads and manages permitted
                            certificate submissions belonging
                            to their assigned organization.
                        </td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>Public Visitor</strong></td>
                        <td>
                            Can access public information
                            and the login page.
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>

            </table>
        </div>

        <p>
            Client accounts are created by an administrator.
            Newly created clients must change their
            temporary password before accessing the portal.
        </p>
    </section>

    <hr />

    @* 6. Съхранявани данни *@
    <section class="mb-4">
        <h3>6. Data Processing & Storage</h3>

        <p>
            To provide its functionality, SecureCert Portal
            stores information such as:
        </p>

        <ul>
            <li>
                Organization names and registration numbers.
            </li>
            <li>
                User names, email addresses, phone numbers,
                departments and job titles when provided.
            </li>
            <li>
                Certificate files and related metadata.
            </li>
            <li>
                Hostnames, submission dates and statuses.
            </li>
            <li>
                Administrative review decisions and comments.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <p>
            User authentication is managed through
            ASP.NET Core Identity. Passwords are stored
            as password hashes, not in plaintext.
        </p>

        <p>
            Uploaded certificate files are stored separately
            from the application's public web directory.
            Certificate metadata and user information
            are maintained in the application database.
        </p>
    </section>

    <hr />

    @* 7. Ограничения и срокове за съхранение *@
    <section class="mb-4">
        <h3>7. Important Limitations</h3>

        <p>
            A successful upload or administrative approval
            should not be interpreted as independent
            confirmation that a certificate is trusted
            by browsers or operating systems.
        </p>

        <p>
            Certificate submission and review records are
            retained according to the application's
            implemented management rules.
            An automatic retention and deletion schedule
            has not yet been configured.
        </p>

        <p>
            Users should contact the portal administrator
            for requests concerning their account,
            stored information or access.
        </p>
    </section>

    <hr />

    @* 8. Насоки за сигурна работа *@
    <section class="mb-4">
        <h3>8. Security Recommendations</h3>

        <ul>
            <li>
                Access the portal using its HTTPS address.
            </li>
            <li>
                Keep account credentials confidential.
            </li>
            <li>
                Never share a temporary password in a URL.
            </li>
            <li>
                Upload public certificates only.
            </li>
            <li>
                Verify the hostname before submission.
            </li>
            <li>
                Sign out when using a shared computer.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <hr />

    @* 9. Връзка към администратора *@
    <section class="mb-4">
        <h3>9. Support</h3>

        <p>
            For account access issues, certificate submission
            questions or data-related requests,
            please contact your SecureCert Portal administrator.
        </p>

        <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2">

            <a asp-controller="Home"
               asp-action="Index"
               class="btn btn-outline-secondary">
                Back to Home
            </a>

            @if (User.Identity?.IsAuthenticated != true)
            {
                <a asp-controller="Account"
                   asp-action="Login"
                   class="btn btn-primary">
                    Sign In
                </a>
            }

        </div>
    </section>

    <p class="text-muted small">
        This page describes the current application
        functionality and security guidelines.
        It is not a complete legal privacy notice.
    </p>

</div>
